>>object oriented programming:
In 60's and 70's programers wrote seprate function and other data's in long projects that made a proggrame dirty,many lined and difficult if one data has eror then programmers take many days to solve simple erors because code contains millions of line and for every programmer to find that erored line is so difficult then programers  make object oriented based programming languages which makes code simple,clean,readable and in some lines it ends easily , they also finds erors easily.                                                                                                
>class:
it is  blue print of objects in our programes we have to just make a class wich have __init__ as constructer of method means first method and methods are nothing same as functions we define method in class it works same as functions just we have to add self in every parameter of these methods and dunder init means __init__ this method is written firstly and we use these same as those functions but we make just some copies method in class and use many objects as we want we can make.                                                                                                                                                                                      
>objects:
we can make different objects just we have to call that class and in parenthesis we have to pass those arguement which our inint method needs and store that in a variable after that we can print any method using  object by writting the name of that variable dot and method name which we need for more explanation you have to examples.                                                                                                  
>instance and class variables:
instance variables are those which are inside methods using self we write them in __init__ function self dot and that variable name = data of that variable and class variable which are written independentely inside class just take variable and assign our data directly but these variable are directlt use for class we dont use objects and that data is permanent for that class we change it only in that variable.                                                                                            
>simple conclusion points:
1. Class is just a blue print, object is real data holder.
2. __init__ automatically runs when object creates.
3. Self is working using that object which we runs.
4. Instance variable are unique for every object runs when we have a object.
5. Class variable having their own data we use it without any object by class.
6. Every method inside our class work based on the data of our object.                                                                                                                                                                                                 
>Encapsulation:
when we use double underscore before a instance variable then that will become encapsulation ,we use that only in that class not out side of class so using encapsulation our programme become secure no one can directly access that value outside of class.                                                                                                         
>Inheritence:
it means we have to create some child classes of a class just we write that parent class name in parenthesis and we can use all methods  of that class easilly.
>pollymorphism:'
it is rellated thing with inheritence when we make child classes then in child class we can eassily change the properties of methods of parent class ust def that method name and use self and directly change and this changing is pollymorphism.
>Abstraction:
if we want to hide the work of method,how behind the scene it works then we  have to just write from abc import ABC ,abstractmethod  in the starting of programme and just one line befoe where we hide we have to use @abstractmethod.
>simple conclusion points:
1. inheritence just create child classes from a parent class
2. pollymorphism just use methods of that parent class and change the behavior of that with same name.
3.abstraction just hide the behind the scene work of a method or class.
